<title>BRAZIL: Brazil Petrobras discovers new gas field.</title>
<headline>Brazil Petrobras discovers new gas field.</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1997-01-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazilian state oil monopoly Petrobras has announced the discovery of new natural gas reserves in the Amazon estimated at five billion cubic meters.</p>
<p>Tests carried out at depths of 2,990 meters (27,000 feet) in the Solimoes river basin revealed a potential production capacity of 220,000 cubic meters of gas per day and 325 barrels of light oil (condensate) per day.</p>
<p>((--Simona de Logu, Rio de Janeiro newsroom, 5521 507 4151))</p>
